  <h1>Automated Database Migrations with Alembic & AWS RDS</h1>
  <p>PostgreSQL on AWS RDS with schema versioning using Python's Alembic and SQLAlchemy for reliable cloud-hosted database version control.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>AWS RDS</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>Alembic</span><span>SQLAlchemy</span><span>Python</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/alembic.png" alt="Alembic AWS RDS Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates managing a <strong>PostgreSQL database on AWS RDS</strong> with incremental schema migrations using Alembic — think of it as Git for your database schema.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Launched a <strong>PostgreSQL RDS instance</strong> using AWS CLI.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>Alembic with SQLAlchemy and psycopg2</strong> to connect Python to RDS.</li>
      <li>Created and applied <strong>migration scripts</strong> to add and manage database tables.</li>
      <li>Verified migrations using the <strong>psql client</strong>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>☁️ AWS Layer</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>RDS PostgreSQL</strong> — Cloud-hosted database</li>
          <li>Configured via <strong>AWS CLI</strong></li>
          <li>Automated backups enabled</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🐍 Python Stack</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>SQLAlchemy</strong> — ORM for schema definitions</li>
          <li><strong>Alembic</strong> — Migration version control</li>
          <li><strong>psycopg2</strong> — PostgreSQL driver</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔍 Verification</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>psql client</strong> — Inspect created tables</li>
          <li>Alembic tracks migrations like Git commits</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Launched and configured an <strong>AWS RDS PostgreSQL</strong> database using AWS CLI.</li>
      <li>Understood how Alembic tracks migrations like <strong>Git commits for databases</strong>.</li>
      <li>Created and applied multiple migration scripts (e.g., <code>account</code>, <code>account2</code> tables).</li>
      <li>Verified migrations using the <strong>psql client</strong>.</li>
      <li>Gained experience integrating Python tools with cloud databases.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Manage credentials securely via <strong>AWS Secrets Manager</strong>.</li>
      <li>Restrict security groups — <strong>PostgreSQL port 5432</strong> to trusted IPs only.</li>
      <li>Maintain <strong>separate migration histories</strong> per environment (dev/staging/prod).</li>
      <li>Enable <strong>automated backups and monitoring</strong> on RDS instances.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

